*7:30 a.m., Sept. 8, County of Kaua=CA=BBi, Hurricane Lowell Update*

L=C4=AAHU=CA=BBE =E2=80=93 Hurricane Lowell brought damaging winds, heavy r=
ain, and high surf to Kaua=CA=BBi overnight, passing west of the island ear=
ly Tuesday. Widespread power outages, downed trees, and debris have been re=
ported islandwide, along with damage from wind and coastal surge.


The public is urged to stay indoors and keep off roads to allow crews to as=
sess damage, clear debris, and restore power and services safely.

Do not drive through flooded roadways or around barricades, and stay away f=
rom downed power lines.

Residents are urged to closely document damage to their homes and property.

A damage assessment form is available through the Kaua=CA=BBi Emergency Man=
agement Agency website at=C2=A0https://survey123.arcgis.com/share/54d0b90fb=
