*The Kaua=CA=BBi Department of Water*

The Kaua=CA=BBi Department of Water has issued an islandwide conservation n=
otice. Customers are asked to limit water use to essential needs while crew=
s work to maintain service during power outages. Report outages, low pressu=
re, or water main breaks to DOW at 808-245-5400, or visit kauaiwater.org.


  * Power outages can affect pumps and wells. Water service may be interrup=
ted or pressure may drop, even if your home is not damaged.=20
  * Use water sparingly while storm response and utility repairs are ongoin=
g.=20
  * Do not use water you suspect has been contaminated by flooding.=20
  * Report outages, low pressure, or water main breaks to DOW at 808-245-54=
00.=20
  * Updates will be posted at kauaiwater.org and on DOW=E2=80=99s social me=
dia channels.=20

*Road Closures*

Numerous roads are closed islandwide due to storm-related debris and damage=
, including portions of Kaumuali=CA=BBi Highway and K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway=
. Closures include:


  * K=C5=ABhi=C5=8D Highway at the Hanalei Bridge=20
  * Kaumuali=CA=BBi Highway between the Kala Road junctions and Akialoa Roa=
d=20
  * M=C4=81luhia Road at Kaumuali=CA=BBi Highway=20

Additional closures are expected as the Hawai=CA=BBi State Department of Tr=
ansportation and County Public Works crews assess and clear roadways. Debri=
s has been reported islandwide. Road and closure conditions are available a=
t 808-241-1725.

*Refuge Areas*

As of 6:30 a.m., 301 people and 38 pets are being sheltered at the County=
=E2=80=99s five open refuge areas:


  * Kaua=CA=BBi High School Gym, 3577 Lala Road, L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe=20
  * Kal=C4=81heo Neighborhood Center, 4480 Papalina Road, Kal=C4=81heo=20

  * Waimea Canyon Middle School, 9555 Huakai Road, Waimea=20
  * K=C4=ABlauea Neighborhood Center, 2460 Keneke Street, K=C4=ABlauea=20

  * Kapa=CA=BBa Middle School, 4867 Olohena Road, Kapa=CA=BBa=20

Refuge areas remain open. Anyone going to a refuge area should bring their =
own disaster supply go-kit, medications, and important documents. Household=
 pets are welcome, though owners must bring their own pet food, water, and =
crates or cages. Do not travel to a refuge area if conditions are unsafe.

*Facility Closures*


  * All County, State, and Department of Education offices and schools are =
closed Tuesday, Sept. 8.=20
  * L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe Airport closed at 2:30 p.m. Monday, Sept. 7, until fur=
ther notice, according to the state Department of Transportation. Runway an=
d facility inspections are required before flights resume. Travelers should=
 contact their airlines directly.=20
  * Refuse collection service is suspended until further notice.=20
  * The Kaua=CA=BBi Bus suspended service due to safety concerns. Buses had=
 been supporting transportation to refuge areas.=20
  * All County parks, campgrounds, and the Wailua Golf Course are closed un=
til further notice.=20
  * All Department of Land and Natural Resources state parks and state fore=
st reserves are closed until further notice.=20
  * The Pacific Missile Range Facility has closed its recreational guest pa=
ss program and recreational sites until further notice.=20
  * The state Department of Health has issued an islandwide brown water adv=
isory for Kaua=CA=BBi. Stay out of floodwaters and ocean water near stream =
mouths, drainage outlets, and harbors, which may contain sewage, animal was=
te, chemicals, and debris.=20
  * The Ocean Safety Bureau advises no swimming or outdoor recreational act=
ivities until further notice.=20

*Weather Notices in Effect*


  * Hurricane Warning =E2=80=93 Kaua=CA=BBi and Ni=CA=BBihau.=20
  * Flood Watch=20
  * High Surf Warning=20

Warnings and watches may be extended, dropped, or modified as conditions de=
velop.

*Other important numbers and resources*

To stay updated, tune in to local media broadcast channels for the most cur=
rent information. The following resources are available for emergency prepa=
redness:


  * Kaua=CA=BBi Emergency Management Agency =E2=80=93 kauai.gov/KEMA=20
  * National Weather Service =E2=80=93 weather.gov/hfo, or automated weathe=
r line at 808-245-6001=20
  * Kaua=CA=BBi Department of Water =E2=80=93 808-245-5400 and kauaiwater.o=
rg=20
  * Road and closure conditions =E2=80=93 808-241-1725=20

Officials remind the public to use 9-1-1 only for life-threatening or time-=
critical emergencies. Calls to 9-1-1 for weather updates or general road co=
nditions can significantly delay emergency response. To report non-emergenc=
y road hazards, contact KPD Dispatch (non-emergency) at 808-241-1711.

For up-to-date information about Kaua=CA=BBi ocean conditions and safety, p=
lease speak to a county lifeguard, visit safebeachday.com, or call the Ocea=
n Safety Bureau at 808-241-4984.

To sign up for Everbridge, the County=E2=80=99s emergency notification serv=
ice, please visit www.kauai.gov/KEMA and click =E2=80=9CNotification Servic=
es.=E2=80=9D You may also text =E2=80=9CKAUAIEMA=E2=80=9D to 888777, or cal=
l the Kaua=CA=BBi Emergency Management Agency at 808-241-1800.

